Bogotá
pos: prop
  meta: {{es-proper noun|f}}
  g: f
  etymology: From an unattested Chibcha word variously described as the name of the surrounding region, the capital of the Muisca Confederation, the original name of the town of Funza, the name of a Muisca cacique or his title.\n\nVarious forms have been proposed as the original name, such as Bacatá (possibly a later invention ); Bocatá, meaning “fields’ end” and the name of a cacique; Bogote, referring to the Bogotá Savannah and used as a hereditary title; Muequetá, supposedly from Chibcha "muyquy" (“field”) + ta (“inside; field”).
  gloss: Bogota, Bogotá (a capital city of Colombia)
    syn: (historical; official from 1991 to 2000) Santafé de Bogotá
