  meta: {{es-proper noun|m}}
  g: m
  etymology: Ramiro and Ramira stem from a Gothic "*𐍂𐌰𐌽𐌰𐌼𐌴𐍂𐍃" / *𐍂𐌰𐌽𐌰𐌼𐌴𐍂𐌴𐌹𐍃, latinised as Ranamirus or Ramirus. The Gothic name consists of Proto-Germanic "*rana-" (“corner, wedge”) (compare Old English "rand" (“edge, rim”)) and *mēraz / *mērijaz (“famous”).\nCognates include Catalan "Ramir".
  gloss: given name
