ajonjolí
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "ajonjolí", aljonjolí, from an ambiguous Andalusian Arabic form, of raised final vowel from Arabic "جُلْجُلَان" (“sesame seed”), or of clipped ending, جُلْجُل  + -í, as the descendants of the pomegranate cultivar سَفَرِيّ, or rather  + -ín in view of Portuguese "gergelim" (“sesame”), all of which require dissimilation in the second consonant of the Romance form. Instances of metathetic جُنْجُلَال can also be found today, the last consonant of which would only have undergone haplology after a raise of the vowel before it.
  gloss: sesame (tropical Asian plant Sesamum indicum)
    syn: sésamo
  gloss: sesame, sesame seed (the seed of this plant)
