  usage: The difference between anillo and anilla: both translate as ring in English. Anillo is for the jewellery, also the planetary ring, ring on a tree, bullfighting ring, building in a circular shape, geometrical ring, among others. Anilla may refer to a curtain ring, ring on a shoe, a ring onto which to tie a rope, a ring put round a bird's foot for tracking (also known as anillo), a gymnastic ring, among others.
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "aniello", from Latin "ānellum" (“little ring”), from ānulus, diminutive of ānus (“ring”). Compare Catalan "anell", French "anneau", Italian "anello", Portuguese "anel".
