antiguo
pos: adj
  meta: {{es-adj|sup=antiquísimo}}
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "antigo", from Latin "antīquus" (variant form antīcus). The form antiguo in Spanish was probably the result of influence from the feminine form antigua on the older antigo. Compare Ladino "antigo", Portuguese "antigo", Catalan "antic", Italian "antico". Cf. Old French "antif", which was also influenced by its feminine form antive (both replaced in modern French by a borrowed form antique).
  gloss: old, former, erstwhile, quondam, one-time, onetime
    syn: anterior; ex
  gloss: old, ancient, age-old
    syn: viejo
  gloss: vintage, antique
    syn: vintage
  gloss: old-fashioned, outdated, old-style, old-time
    syn: anticuado; pasado de moda
  gloss: long-standing, longstanding
    syn: de larga data
