banana
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|f}}
  g: f
  usage: banana may also be used in Spain, to differentiate from plátano (“plantain”); otherwise, plátano refers to either.
  etymology: Derived from a nic language spoken in the Guinea region, probably through Portuguese "banana". Further derivation is Uncertain. Possible ancestor or cognate languages include Wolof "banaana", Eastern Maninkakan "banana", and Vai "ꕒꘌꕯ" or ꕒꕌꕯ. However, Ay Baati Wolof (Munro & Gaye, 1997) posits that Wolof "banaana" is itself derived from Portuguese "banana".
  gloss: banana (fruit)
    q: Rioplatense, Andes, Guatemala, Honduras
    syn: plátano; guineo; cambur; banano
  gloss: an idiot
    q: Uruguay, colloquial
    syn: idiota
  gloss: smartass
    q: Argentina, Dominican Republic, colloquial
    syn: sabihondo
  gloss: penis
    q: Bolivia, Guatemala, Costa Rica, Honduras, colloquial, slang, vulgar
    syn: Thesaurus:pene
