  etymology: Inherited from la-eme "blancus", from Proto-Germanic "*blankaz" (“white, bright, blinding”), from Proto-Indo-European "*bhleg-" (“to shine”). Found as early as the Cantar de Mio Cid.\n\nCompare Old High German "blanch" (“shining, bright, white”) (German "blank"), Old English "blanc" (“white, grey”), blanca (“white steed”). Cognate with English "blank", Dutch "blank", etc.
  gloss: white
    syn: (poetic) albo; (obsolete) obo
  gloss: white (of light skin)
  gloss: argent
    q: heraldry
    syn: argento
