cabrito
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "cabrito". Analyzable as cabra + -ito; may have originally corresponded to a Vulgar Latin or Late Latin "caprītus" (attested in Salic Law), as the perfect passive participle of a verb *caprīre (“give birth (of goats)”), from Latin "caper" (which would have normally yielded *cabrido), but was influenced by the Spanish diminutive suffix -ito (from Late Latin -ittus). Compare Portuguese "cabrito", Aragonese "crabido", crabito, crapito, Catalan "cabrit", Occitan "cabrit", dialectal French "chevri".
  gloss: kid (young goat)
_____
