  g: m
  etymology: Uncertain. Likely inherited from Vulgar Latin "*cattulus", from Latin "catŭlus" (“whelp, puppy”), plus the suffix -orro; whence also Portuguese "cachorro". If so, a doublet of cacho.\n\nAn alternative link to Basque "txakur", xakur (“puppy”) has been proposed, but it is often dismissed as speculative.
