  usage: * It is often used to refer to a resident of that same neighborhood who fits a profile that links the individual to a predisposition to conflict or crime, so its use is sometimes derogatory. This usage is usually based on territorial and social prejudices unrelated to the demographic reality of the neighborhood.\n* By extension, also derogatory, it sometimes refers to any person of Arab or Berber origin in Melilla with the stereotype of a "threatening" person or someone linked to a marginalized subculture, implicitly suggesting a predisposition to physical confrontation.
  etymology: Derived from La Cañada + -ero, Ellipsis of "La Cañada de Hidúm", a marginal neighbourhood in Melilla.
