  meta: {{es-adj|sup=chulísimo}}
  usage: Chulo is to define actions and means cute, but in people it means cocky. To describe an action as cocky one uses chulesco. For example, "una jugada chula" means "a cute play" while "una jugada chulesca" means "a cocky play".
  etymology: Borrowed from Italian "ciullo", a now-obsolete shortening of Italian "fanciullo", a diminutive based ultimately on Latin "īnfāns".
  gloss: cute, pretty, lovely, cool, nifty
    q: of actions
    syn: guapo; mono; cuqui; bonito; genial; Thesaurus:guay
  gloss: cocky (overly confident, arrogant and boastful)
    q: Spain, colloquial, of people
