  etymology: Unknown. Coromines and Pascual, citing Eguílaz, suggest a variant of Arabic "كِيس" (“bag”) with the feminine marker ـة, with a metathesis of the consonants that is said to be "frequent" in spoken Arabic, cognate to Moroccan Arabic "كِيسة" (“bag”), and Old Galician-Portuguese "aciqua" (“bag”). First attested in the early 17th century.
  gloss: money bag
    syn: monedero
