  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "cuémpadre", from Late Latin "compatrem", from com- + Latin "pater" (“father”). Dialectal cumpa is a doublet.
  gloss: godfather of one's child
  gloss: parent of one's godchild
  gloss: friend, especially a very close and honoured male friend
  gloss: father of one's child's spouse
