cuajado
pos: adj
  meta: {{es-adj}}
  etymology: Past participle of cuajar. Equivalent to cuajar + -ado. The colloquial meaning is a culinary metaphor: just as a liquid (like milk or beaten eggs) "sets" or coagulates and stops flowing, a person who is cuajado is perceived as mentally "set," slow to react, or lacking energy and initiative.
  gloss: curdled, coagulated, set (of a liquid, such as milk or eggs, that has thickened or solidified)
    q: cooking
  gloss: dazed, slow, clueless, passive; lacking initiative or quick reflexes
    q: Spain, colloquial, derogatory
_____
cuajar
