  meta: {{es-verb}} {{es-conj}}
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "quajar", from Vulgar Latin "*coaglāre/ *quaglāre", from syncopation of Latin "coāgulāre". Doublet of coagular, a borrowing. Compare Aragonese "cuallar", Asturian "cuayar", Catalan "quallar", Galician "callar", French "cailler".
  gloss: to curdle
  gloss: to gel
  gloss: to work (well), to be successfully done, to give results
    q: colloquial
  gloss: to please
    q: colloquial
  gloss: to get filled, to get populated
    q: colloquial
