  usage: * The forms cualquiera and cualesquiera are used after the modified noun. When used before the modified noun, the apocopate forms cualquier and cualesquier are used instead:\n:: cualquier cosa ― whatever thing\n:: una cosa cualquiera ― whatever thing\n* The word is also sometimes used substantively with the noun implied but omitted.
  etymology: From cual (“which”) + quiera (“it may want”).
  gloss: any, whatever, whichever
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  usage: * cualquiera is used preceded by an indefinite article (un, una, unos and unas)\n:: Lo dijo el presidente y no un cualquiera. ― The president said it and not just anybody.
  etymology: From cual (“which”) + quiera (“it may want”).
  gloss: a person of no importance; a nobody, zero
    syn: don nadie; donnadie; mindundi
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|f}}
  g: f
  etymology: From cual (“which”) + quiera (“it may want”).
  gloss: a female prostitute
    q: slang
