culo
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  q: vulgar  in  Latin America, colloquial  in  Spain, anatomy
  usage: In Spain, this term is used colloquially to refer to the buttocks and the vulgarity of the Latin culus was lost, except in offensive idioms like tomar por culo or que te den por el culo. This may be why it isn't labeled as malsonante or vulgar in RAE's dictionary. In Latin America, however, the word is seen as vulgar and possibly offensive. The related word culé, from Catalan culer, which originally meant sodomite, is morphologically related to Spanish culero and is related to the vulgar word cul, which is related to this Spanish word, is not considered vulgar in Spanish.
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "culo", from Latin "culus".
  gloss: ass, arse, booty, rear, behind, butt, buttocks
    syn: trasero; nalgas
  gloss: anus
    syn: ano
  gloss: meaty area around the anus (in various animal species)
  gloss: bottom or end part of certain objects (e.g. glasses, bottles, cucumbers)
    q: usually in the singular
  gloss: liquid remains at the bottom of a container
    q: usually in the singular
    syn: culín; culito
  gloss: partner
    q: vulgar, colloquial, El Salvador
    syn: pareja
  gloss: bunch (a considerable amount)
    q: Peru
