de
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|f}}
  g: f
  gloss: letter: d
pos: prep
  meta: {{head|es|prepositions}}
  usage: * As a rule, de combines with el to form del. The exceptions to this are titles and other proper nouns, e.g. El Dorado, in which case the contraction must be omitted: de El Dorado.\n* May form an all-capital ligature .
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish de, from Latin dē, from Proto-Italic &#42;dē, from Proto-Indo-European &#42;déh₁, from &#42;de + &#42;-h₁. Cognate with Ladino "de".
  gloss: of; 's; used after the thing owned and before the owner
  gloss: from (with the source or provenance of or at)
  gloss: of (expressing composition, substance)
  gloss: about (concerning; with regard to)
    syn: sobre; acerca de
  gloss: of; from (indicating cause)
  gloss: of (indicates a quality or characteristic)
  gloss: from (with the origin, starting point or initial reference of or at)
    syn: desde
  gloss: of (indicates the subject or cause of the adjective)
  gloss: from (with the separation, exclusion or differentiation of)
  gloss: than (in certain phrases)
  gloss: used to construct compound nouns (with attributive nouns)
  gloss: indicates a conditional desire
    q: followed by the infinitive
  gloss: forms adverbs; indicates a time of day or period of someone's life
  gloss: indicates the purpose of an object
    q: after a noun and before a verb
    syn: para
