de nuevo
pos: adv
  meta: {{es-adv}}
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "de nuevo" (“again”), from Latin "dē" (“from”) + novō (“new”), possibly a restructured inherited form of Classical Latin "dēnuō" (“again, anew”), itself a reduced form of a supposed and unattested Old Latin *dē novōd. Related to Medieval Latin dē novō (“afresh, as a new thing, out of nowhere”). Compare French "de nouveau", Italian "di nuovo", di novo, Romanian "din nou".
  gloss: again
    syn: otra vez; nuevamente
  gloss: over again, all over again, all over again from scratch
  gloss: back
