distinto
pos: adj
  meta: {{es-adj}}
  usage: * With a noun phrase (including a relative clause): use the prepositions a or de interchangeably. que is not allowed.\n** distinto a aquellas chicas\n** distinto de eso\n* With a number: use de only.\n** dimensiones distintas de cero\n* When the first term is a whole clause and the second term is a noun: use the conjunction que only.\n** Es distinto beber cerveza que vino\n* With an infinitive clause: both que and a are valid.\n** distinto construir puentes que hablar (normal)\n** distinto a hacerlo en Murcia (also correct)\n* With a clause containing a conjugated (personal) verb:\n** Using que is possible but creates two consecutive ques: distinto que bailés conmigo que que bailés con tu novio.\n** The preferred form to avoid this repetition is a (giving distinto que bailés conmigo a que bailés con tu novio).\n* With a prepositional phrase or an adverb phrase: use que only.\n** distinto en Guipúzcoa que en Vizcaya\n** un tiempo distinto aquí que allí
  etymology: Borrowed from Latin "distīnctus", perfect passive participle of distinguō.
  gloss: distinct
    syn: diferente
pos: adv
  meta: {{es-adv}}
  etymology: Borrowed from Latin "distīnctus", perfect passive participle of distinguō.
  gloss: distinctly
