echar de menos
pos: v
  meta: {{es-verb}}
  etymology: Originally an archaic and dialectal Old Galician-Portuguese idiom, achar (de) menos (“to feel an absence”), entering in Spanish as echar (de) menos (mistaking Old Galician-Portuguese "achar" (“to find”) (Spanish "hallar"), with echar (“to throw”), both verbs pronounced similarly and both of them with a multitude of idioms).
  gloss: to miss; to feel the absence of
    q: idiomatic, Spain, otherwise formal
    syn: (most common in Latin America) extrañar; echar en falta
