_____
el sábado, sabadete, camisa nueva y polvete
pos: phrase
  meta: {{head|es|phrase}}
  etymology: (literally: Saturday, Saturday, new shirt and powder). Traditionally, before the days of washing machines, men would wash their shirt only once a week (Saturday). The polvete (powder) refers to the talcum powder used to clean the shirt. The word sabadete may have originally been a nonce word coined in order to rhyme with polvete.\n\nOver the years, polvo has acquired a slang meaning of sexual intercourse, so the phrase has come to carry connotations of weekend sexual liaisons.
  gloss: a phrase used to show excitement about the day being Saturday; thank God it's the weekend
    q: idiomatic, Spain
_____
