esconder
pos: v
  meta: {{es-verb}} {{es-conj}}
  usage: * Esconder is a false friend and does not mean to ensconce.\nThe Spanish word for to ensconce is instalarse.
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "esconder", from an original asconder  (with a replacement of the prefix with es-), from Latin "abscondere". It formerly showed the expected diphthongization of stressed short Latin /o/ in rhizotonic conjugations (see older escuendo), but this was later levelled out by analogy with arrhizotonic conjugations.\n\nDoublet of absconder and cognate with English "abscond".
  gloss: to hide
    q: transitive, reflexive
    syn: ocultar; escusar
