frutifantástico
pos: adj
  meta: {{es-adj}}
  etymology: From fruta ("fruit") + -i- + fantástico ("fantastic"). It originated from Froot Loops' ads broadcast in Latin America in the late 2000s, in which the narrator creates words by prefixing "fruti-" (a pun on "froot") to different adjectives (frutidivertido, frutifantástico). \n\nThe noun sense is derived from the adjective and emerged from a meme posted on July 11, 2019 on Facebook.
  gloss: fantastic [from late 2000s]
    q: Internet slang, neologism, humorous
