gafas
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|f-p}}
  g: f-p
  etymology: Unknown. Likely from Catalan "gafa" (“hook”) (related to Catalan "agafar"), possibly referring to the hooks that kept eyeglasses in place and differentiated it from a pince-nez. Cognate with English "gaff", meaning a large metal hook. \n\nOther possible etymologies relate it to French "faire gaffe" (“pay attention”), or German "gaffen" (“to stare”).\n\nIt is sometimes said to instead be related to the Andalusian Arab scholar of the 12th century Muhammad ibn Aslam Al-Ghafiqi, an ophthalmologist.
  gloss: eyeglasses
    q: chiefly Spain, some countries in  Latin America
    syn: (Latin America) lentes; (Cuba, Puerto Rico) espejuelos; (Latin America) anteojos
