guapo
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  etymology: Ultimately from Latin "vappa" (“flat wine, worthless person”), probably through the intermediate of dialectal Old French, namely Picard "vape", wape, gape (“dull, insipid (of food); weakened (of people); deranged (of the stomach)”), which has possibly, but not necessarily received influence from Proto-Germanic "*hwapjaną" (“to breathe, air out, let go to waste, become sour”), whereas modern French "gouape" is a reloan from Spanish. At one point the word meant “rascal, ruffian” and evolved in meaning over time.
  gloss: arrowroot
    syn: maranta; sagú; planta obediente
pos: adj
  meta: {{es-adj|sup=guapísimo}}
  etymology: Ultimately from Latin "vappa" (“flat wine, worthless person”), probably through the intermediate of dialectal Old French, namely Picard "vape", wape, gape (“dull, insipid (of food); weakened (of people); deranged (of the stomach)”), which has possibly, but not necessarily received influence from Proto-Germanic "*hwapjaną" (“to breathe, air out, let go to waste, become sour”), whereas modern French "gouape" is a reloan from Spanish. At one point the word meant “rascal, ruffian” and evolved in meaning over time.
  gloss: good-looking; handsome, pretty (describes a man or a woman)
    syn: bonito; hermoso; lindo
  gloss: smart or elegant
  gloss: cool
    q: colloquial, Spain
    syn: guay; Thesaurus:guay
