güey
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  etymology: Nonstandard pronunciation-spelling variant of buey (see that entry for more); this form thus represents a shifting of /bw/ back to /ɡw/. Compare nonstandard güeno from bueno (“good”), agüelo from abuelo (“grandfather”), güelvo from vuelvo (“to return”), where /bwe/ becomes /ɡwe/. A similar phenomenon occurs in the dialectal pronunciation of buvai as /ɡwuei/.
  gloss: chump, punk, dumbass, idiot, jerk
    q: Mexico, colloquial
    syn: cabrón; tonto
  gloss: dude, guy, buddy
    q: Mexico, in the  RD  used  in the vocative, colloquial
    syn: (Mexico) carnal; (Mexico) cuate; (Spain) tío; (Spain) tía; Thesaurus:tío
  gloss: pronunciation spelling of "buey"
    q: Rioplatense, Paraguay
