haba
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|f}}
  g: f
  usage: * The feminine noun haba is like other feminine nouns starting with a stressed a sound in that it takes the definite article el (normally reserved for masculine nouns) in the singular when there is no intervening adjective:\n:: el haba\n* However, if an adjective, even one that begins with a stressed a sound such as alta or ancha, intervenes between the article and the noun, the article reverts to la.
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "faba", from Latin "faba", from Proto-Indo-European "*bʰabʰ-" (“bean”). Cognate with English "fava".
