hacer
pos: v
  meta: {{es-verb}} {{es-conj}} {{es-conj|hacerse}}
  usage: * For the sense of "ago" (e.g. "hace tres días" or "hace mucho que..."), see hace.\n{{U:es:words for become}}
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "fazer", from Latin "facere".\n\nThe first-person indicative (hago) and present subjunctive forms (haga, hagas etc.) may have been influenced by agō (compare English gesture), but more likely come from a voicing of intervocalic Latin /k/ after having dropped /i/ (e.g. faciō > [ˈfa.ko] > hago).
  gloss: to do, perform, execute, carry out
    q: transitive
    _gloss: Forms ad hoc verbs from borrowed nouns
      q: transitive
  gloss: to make
    _gloss: to create, to build, to bring forth
      q: transitive
    _gloss: to write, to compose
      q: transitive
    _gloss: to prepare (food)
      q: transitive
  gloss: in various expressions about the weather
    q: transitive, impersonal, idiomatic
  gloss: to release, to excrete
    q: transitive
  gloss: to prep, adorn, do (a body part)
    q: transitive
  gloss: to make, to cause to be
    q: transitive
  gloss: to make, to cause to
    q: transitive
  gloss: to play (a character)
    q: ambitransitive, optionally with de
  gloss: to become; to get
    q: reflexive, ditransitive, with words that use ser
    syn: volverse; convertirse en
    _gloss: used with time
      q: impersonal, reflexive, ditransitive
  gloss: to pretend being, play
    q: reflexive, ambitransitive
  gloss: to move (over), scoot (over) [+para (direction)]
    q: reflexive
  gloss: ellipsis of "hacerse el tonto"
    q: reflexive, Argentina
  gloss: to get used to (chiefly in idioms)
    q: reflexive, intransitive  with a
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "fazer", from Latin "facere".\n\nThe first-person indicative (hago) and present subjunctive forms (haga, hagas etc.) may have been influenced by agō (compare English gesture), but more likely come from a voicing of intervocalic Latin /k/ after having dropped /i/ (e.g. faciō > [ˈfa.ko] > hago).
  gloss: task, action
    syn: quehacer; acción
