hacer daño
pos: v
  meta: {{es-verb}}
  usage: This verb and (in its transitive sense) lastimar are different from doler in that doler refers to pain and hacer daño/lastimar refers to injury. "Me dolió la pierna" means you felt pain in your leg (your leg hurt) and "Me hice daño en la pierna" means your leg got injured (you hurt your leg). Both hacer daño and lastimar can be used in a figurative sense: "Eso lastimó su reputación" / "Eso (le) hizo daño a su reputación" ("That hurt his/her/their reputation").
  etymology: Compare Catalan "fer mal".
  gloss: to hurt, injure (physically, mentally, etc.) [+en (part of something/someone being hurt)]
    q: reflexive or pronominal
    syn: lastimar; herir
