hache
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|f}}
  g: f
  usage: Nominally, hache always takes the usual feminine articles la and una (la hache, una hache). This makes it an exception to the rule according to which feminine nouns beginning with stressed /ˈa/ frequently take the articles el and un otherwise reserved for masculine nouns (e.g., el alma, un alma).
  etymology: Borrowed from Old French "ache", from Vulgar Latin "*acca".
  gloss: letter: h
