hacia
pos: prep
  meta: {{head|es|preposition}}
  usage: Often replaced with the prepositions a or more colloquially para.
  etymology: According to Coromines and Pascual, from Old Spanish "fazia" (attested ca. 1300), with the variant faza (att. in Cid, Berceo, Calila e Dimna), and in pre-literary Latinized spelling faze ad (att. 1208, in a legal document), from Latin "faciem ad" (facing towards). Unlike in faz, the final -e of Latin faciem was conserved due to appearing in an established phrase, cf. Spanish "pese a" and its variant pesia. Cognate with Leonese "faza".
  gloss: toward, towards
  gloss: around, about (indicating time)
