hembrismo
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  usage: hembrismo is usually employed by antifeminists to describe feminism, in a not offensive manner, unlike its synonym feminazismo. Some people who consider themselves feminists also use it to express their disagreement with certain female chauvinist ideas or behaviours which some people have, and are usually claimed to be part of feminism.
  etymology: From hembra ("female") + -ismo, by analogy with machismo (“male chauvinism”), from macho (“male”).
