  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "encienso", a semi-learned borrowing from Late Latin "incēnsum" (“incense”), from Latin "incēnsus" (“inflamed, fiery”), from incendō (“to set on fire, burn, kindle”). Compare with Old Spanish encensar (“to cense”) and enceso (“inflamed, kindled”) (from encender), which was inherited directly from Latin.
  gloss: incense
  gloss: Myrocarpus frondosus, a tree from the Fabaceae family
