limón
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  usage: Not all countries make a distinction between 'lime' and 'lemon'; limón may be used for both. Where this is the case, 'lime' is usually the default reading (except in Spain), and they may be distinguished as limón verde (lime) and limón amarillo (lemon), or simply as limón (lime) and limón amarillo (lemon) - in much of North America - or limón (lemon) and limón verde (lime) in Spain. In Mexico and much of South America, lima may be used for 'lemon', while in Spain, lima is commonly used for 'lime'.
  etymology: Borrowed from Arabic "لَيْمُون" via Andalusian Arabic, from Persian "لیمو", لیمون, from Sanskrit "निम्बू". By surface analysis, lima + -ón.
  gloss: lemon (fruit)
