pos: adj
  meta: {{head|es|adjective form|g=m|apocopate||standard form|malo}}
  g: m
  usage: The form mal is used only before and within the noun phrase of singular masculine noun. In other positions, malo is used instead:\n: Fue un mal viaje. ― It was a bad trip.\n: El viaje fue malo. ― The trip was bad.\n: Él es un escritor malo. ― He is a bad writer.
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "mal,malo", from Latin "malus", possibly derived from Proto-Indo-European "*(s)mel-" (“bad, wrong”).
  gloss: apocopic form of "malo" bad; evil
    q: before the noun
  gloss: amiss, awry, off, wrong
