  meta: {{es-noun|m|f=+}}
  g: m
  etymology: Inherited from Vulgar Latin "*pectinī̆culum", diminutive of Latin "pecten" (“pubic hair; comb”). The unexpected /nd/ may be due to the influence of pender (“hang down, dangle”). Compare Portuguese "pentelho".
  gloss: pubic hair (a single hair growing in the pubic region)
