plomo
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m}}
  g: m
  etymology: From Latin plumbum. The initial group <pl-> usually became <ll-> in inherited Spanish, so a fully popular development would give *llomo or similar. The form plomo points to a semi-learned term taken early from Latin, or to a borrowing through medieval - (see plom) or -. A - origin is unlikely, since the expected - form would be *plombo, although the region is relevant because most of the lead in Spain came from Almería in Andalusia. A conservative pronunciation might have persisted among educated speakers, which would also explain the retention of <pl-> as, compare also plaza; there is also retention of <cl-> in words such as claro.{{ref|}}
  gloss: lead (heavy, pliable, inelastic metal)
  gloss: grey (colour between white and black)
  gloss: shot, pellet
  gloss: plumb line
  gloss: fuse
  gloss: bore, drag (something boring or dull)
    q: informal
