por qué
pos: adv
  meta: {{es-adv}}
  usage: por qué is used when asking questions ("why") and porque is used when giving answers ("because"). porqué is a noun derived from por qué which means "reason". Because por que can be a combination of the preposition por and the relative pronoun que, it can also be translated as "why", for example in "Esa es la razón por (la) que hice eso." ("That's the reason (why) I did that.") (literally: "That's the reason for which I did that" or "That's the reason due to which I did that").
  etymology: From por (“for”) + qué (“what”). Compare porque (“because”), porqué (“a reason why”) and por que.
  gloss: why, for what reason
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|m|por qués}}
  g: m
  etymology: From por (“for”) + qué (“what”). Compare porque (“because”), porqué (“a reason why”) and por que.
  gloss: misspelling of "porqué"
