qué
pos: determiner
  meta: {{head|es|determiner}}
  etymology: Inherited from Latin quid.
  gloss: (see usage notes) what; which
    syn: cuál (Latin America)
  gloss: what a; such
    q: exclamative
pos: adv
  meta: {{es-adv}}
  etymology: Inherited from Latin quid.
  gloss: how
    q: exclamative
  gloss: Replaces an interrogative word like cómo, cuándo, etc
    q: Spain, nonstandard
pos: pron
  meta: {{head|es|pronoun|cat2=interrogative pronouns}}
  etymology: Inherited from Latin quid.
  gloss: what
pos: interj
  meta: {{head|es|interjection}}
  usage: * Qué and cuál should not be confused with que and cual.\n* Usually, qué and cuál are translated into English as what and which, respectively. There are a few exceptions to this general rule that often trip up learners.\n*: In questions with the verb ser (“to be”), qué is used to ask about definitions of things:\n*:: ¿Qué es un nombre? ― What is a name? (What does "name" mean?)\n*: If the question with ser is not about a definition, cuál is used:\n*:: ¿Cuál es tu nombre? ― What is your name?\n*: If qué was used here, the question would be understood to be about the literal definition of the name, like asking "What does your name mean?". More examples:\n*:: ¿Cuál es la capital de Francia? ― What is the capital of France?\n*:: ¿Cuál es el problema aquí? ― What is the problem here?\n*: Before a noun, qué and cuál are interchangeable and synonymous (except in exclamations, such as "¡Qué lástima!" (What a pity!), where only qué is used).\n*:: ¿Qué/cuál libro estás leyendo? ― What book are you reading?\n*:: ¿Qué/cuál respuesta crees que es la correcta? ― Which answer do you think is correct?\n*:: Dime a qué/cuáles países te gustaría viajar. ― Tell me which countries you would like to visit.\n*: In Spain, however, cuál is rarely used before a noun, and qué is typically used instead.\n\n:: As mentioned, only qué is used as a determiner or adverb in exclamations, and it can be translated in many ways depending on the sentence.
  etymology: Inherited from Latin quid.
  gloss: what (expresses surprise or confusion)
    syn: cómo
_____
qué bolá
pos: phrase
  meta: {{head|es|phrase|head=¿[[qué]] [[bolá]]?}}
  gloss: what's up; 'sup
    q: Cuba
