  meta: {{es-adj|sup=sencillísimo}}
  usage: A way to think of the difference between sencillo and simple, which both mean "simple" in English, is that the antonym of sencillo is complicado (“complicated”), whereas the antonym of simple is complejo (“complex”).
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "senziello", from Vulgar Latin "*singellus", from Latin "singulus". Compare Portuguese "singelo", Catalan "senzill", Asturian "cenciellu". See also sendos, which was inherited directly from Latin singulus.
  gloss: plain
    syn: llano
  gloss: simple, straightforward
    syn: franco
pos: n
