  gloss: mister, sir, lord (title conferred on a married or older male)
    syn: Sr.; Sr
  gloss: gentleman
    syn: caballero
  gloss: master
    syn: amo
pos: adj
  meta: {{es-adj}}
  etymology: From señor in the sense of mister, a title which gives importance to men and signals their social status; from there it was applied to masculine nouns in order to achieve a similar effect with them. Compare Portuguese "senhor#Adjective".
  gloss: great big; whopping
    q: prepositive
  gloss: free
