so
pos: prep
  meta: {{head|es|preposition}}
  usage: So is very rare in modern Spanish, surviving only in certain expressions, including so pena de (“on pain of, under penalty of”), so pretexto de or so color de (“under pretext of”), a so capa (“secretly, with bribery”).
  etymology: Inherited from Latin "sub", from Proto-Italic "*supo", from Proto-Indo-European "*upo".
  gloss: under
    q: archaic
    syn: debajo de; bajo
pos: adv
  meta: {{es-adv}}
  etymology: Abbreviation of seó (“Sir”).
  gloss: blithering, bloody
