  etymology: From Latin "sonus", probably through the intermediate of Old Occitan "son" (or influenced by it); alternatively, but less likely, regressively derived from the verb sonar (the more expected form is sueno that appeared in some Medieval texts). Compare English "sound" and Portuguese "som".
