tacha
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|f}}
  g: f
  etymology: Borrowed from Vulgar Latin "*tacca", *tecca, of gem origin, from Gothic "𐍄𐌰𐌹𐌺𐌽𐍃" (“mark, sign”), from Proto-Germanic "*taiknaz", *taikniz (“sign, mark”), from Proto-Indo-European "*deyḱ-". \n\nInfluenced by forms related to Frankish "to stick, attach" and Gothic "𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌺𐍃" (“mark”). See attacher. Cognate with Old High German "zeihhan" (“sign, symbol, feature”), Old English "tācn" (“sign, marker”). More at token.
  gloss: fault, blemish
    syn: falta; defecto; imperfección; deficiencia; falla; mancha
  gloss: any cross out sign (/, \, —, or X)
  gloss: a type of small nail
  gloss: A legal argument for doubting a witness's testimony
    q: law
  gloss: an ecstasy pill; MDMA
    q: slang
