  etymology: From metathesis of Late Latin "titulāre", a verb based on Latin "titulus". Alternatively formed in Spanish based on tilde. In either case, likely semi-learned or an early borrowing, considering the /i/ for Latin /ĭ/. Doublet of titular.
  gloss: to declare or brand as; to stigmatize
  gloss: to put a tilde or other accent mark over
  gloss: hang (of a computer, to stop working)
    q: reflexive, informal
  gloss: to go into a trance, a stupor
    q: reflexive, informal
