tilde
pos: n
  meta: {{es-noun|f,m<q:chiefly Uruguay>}}
  g: f; m<q:chiefly Uruguay>
  usage: In Spanish, the term tilde refers to a diacritic in general (including the tilde on top of ñ) but it is primarily used to designate the acute accent, as in á. The term virgulilla is used to specifically refer to the tilde on top of ñ. In Spain, outside of technical contexts, it only means acute accent. Another word for acute accent in Latin America is acento.
  etymology: Deverbal of "tildar" or from Latin "titulus", possibly through an Old Catalan or Old Provençal intermediate (accounting for the final -e instead of -o).
  gloss: diacritic
  gloss: acute accent
    syn: (chiefly Latin America) acento; (technical) acento ortográfico
  gloss: tilde
    syn: virgulilla
  gloss: criticism, censure
