traidor
pos: adj
  meta: {{es-adj}}
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "traydor", traïdor, traedor, related to traer (“to betray”) and perhaps a semi-learned borrowing from Latin "trāditōrem" (“traitor, betrayer”) (the main evidence being its use with a hiatus -aï- in Berceo), from trādō, trādere (“to hand over, abandon something”), from trāns (“across, beyond”) + dō (“to give”).
  gloss: traitorous (characteristic of a traitor)
    syn: traicionero
  gloss: unpredictable
    syn: impredecible
pos: n
