pos: pron
  meta: {{head|es|pronoun|disjunctive|ti|oblique|te|comitative|contigo|preposed possessive determiner|tu|possessive pronoun/postposed or standalone possessive determiner|tuyo}}
  usage: * When more pronouns are included in the same sentence, it is considered impolite to say the pronoun yo at first, it must be the last one, and tú must be said after any third person (this applies also for ti and mí):\n** Iremos Rosa, tú y yo. ― Rosa, you and I will go.
  etymology: Inherited from Latin "tū", from Proto-Italic "*tū", from Proto-Indo-European "*túh₂". Cognate with English "thou", Portuguese "tu", Catalan "tu", French "tu", Italian "tu", Romanian "tu".
  gloss: you (second-person singular pronoun)
