vos
pos: pron
  meta: {{head|es|pronoun|oblique|te|preposed possessive determiner|tu|possessive pronoun/postposed or standalone possessive determiner|tuyo}}
  usage: * In Argentina, Uruguay, and Paraguay, tú is almost completely replaced with vos.\n* In the other highlighted countries, the use of vos alternates with tuteo in more formal situations.\n* In Nicaragua, tú is only occasionally used.\n* In Colombia, vos is used in the Paisa region and in the Valle del Cauca, La Guajira, Nariño, southern Cauca, northern Tolima, and northern Cesar departments.
  etymology: Inherited from Latin "vōs" (“you, plural”), from itc-ola "vōs", from Proto-Italic "*wōs".
  gloss: you, familiar form of the second-person singular pronoun
    q: Argentina, Uruguay, Paraguay, Bolivia, Chile, Central America, Chiapas, Zulia, parts of  Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and  the  Philippines
    syn: tú
  gloss: an elevated form of you, either singular or plural
    q: archaic
