ya
pos: adv
  meta: {{es-adv}}
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "ya" (“already; now”), from Latin "iam". Compare Ladino "ya", Asturian "yá", Galician "xa", Portuguese "já", Catalan "ja", French "déjà" and Italian "già".
  gloss: (in the present or imperative) now, right now, (in the negative) anymore, no longer
    _gloss: by now, at this point
  gloss: (in the past) indicates completion of an action (difference from sense 4 depends on context)
  gloss: yet (in questions)
  gloss: already
  gloss: at some point in the future, later, eventually, soon, then, afterwards
  gloss: immediately
    syn: ya mismo; ahora mismo; ahorita
  gloss: only
    q: in negatives, regional
pos: conj
  meta: {{head|es|conjunction|head=ya ... ya ...}}
  etymology: Inherited from Old Spanish "ya" (“already; now”), from Latin "iam". Compare Ladino "ya", Asturian "yá", Galician "xa", Portuguese "já", Catalan "ja", French "déjà" and Italian "già".
  gloss: first (something) then (something else); first (something), now (something else)
  gloss: whether (something) or (something else)
pos: interj
  meta: {{head|es|interjection}}
