⸘ ‽
pos: symbol
  meta: {{head|es|punctuation mark|head=[[⸘]] [[‽]]|cat2=matched pairs}}
  usage: The same effect is more commonly achieved with both sets of punctuation marks one inside the other: ¿¡Verdad!? or ¡¿Verdad?! Older usage, still official but not widespread, recommended mixing the punctuation marks: ¡Verdad? or ¿Verdad!
  etymology: * ⸘: Superimposition of ¡ and ¿.\n* ‽: Superimposition of ! and ?.
  gloss: encloses an emphatic question
    q: uncommon
